AIM:
To find nth Fibonacci number using recursion and iteration.

ALGORITHM;
Read n
If recursive → fib(n)=fib(n-1)+fib(n-2)
If iterative → loop and compute
Print result

PROGARM:
#include<stdio.h>
int fib(int n)
{
    if(n<=1)
        return n;
    return fib(n-1)+fib(n-2);
}
int main()
{
    int n,i,a=0,b=1,c;
    printf("Enter n: ");
    scanf("%d",&n);
    printf("Recursive Fibonacci: %d\n", fib(n));
    printf("Iterative series:\n");
    for(i=0;i<n;i++)
    {
        printf("%d ",a);
        c=a+b;
        a=b;
        b=c;
    }
}

OUTPUT:
Enter n: 6
Recursive Fibonacci: 8
Iterative series:
0 1 1 2 3 5


RESULT:
Thus nth Fibonacci number is obtained using recursion and iteration.
